# Response headers for every file of the app, applied by Cloudflare's static assets (wr.py ships this file).
# The page is never shown inside another site's frame, the browser doesn't guess file types, and other sites
# are told only this origin, never a full address.
#
# Content-Security-Policy: the app runs only its own scripts and styles (no inline code; el() sets styles
# through element.style, which the policy allows), and talks only to: the sync worker (js/config.js), Planning
# Center's API, the account server and Ask Guardian (sixthdaystudios.com), and the three AI providers
# (js/ai.js). Adding a new outside service means adding its origin here, or the browser blocks it.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://rosterwarden-sync.mikey-257.workers.dev https://api.planningcenteronline.com https://sixthdaystudios.com https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com https://api.anthropic.com https://api.openai.com; frame-src https://sixthdaystudios.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
